### (1) is every point of B near one of the six permutations of (1/4,1/2,3/4)? ###
  sampled points of B: 260 ; sup-distance to the nearest of the six centres:
    min 0.0056   median 0.0333   max 0.0917
  all within 1/8 = 0.125 of a centre : True

### (2) the box radius implied by the volume ###
  |B| = 0.003367 ; six boxes of half-width rho gives 6*(2 rho)^3 = |B| -> rho = 0.0412
  observed max distance 0.0917 is the same order

### (3) the centre-hitting criterion ###
  hitting (1/4,1/2,3/4) needs d2 u = -1/4, d3 u = -1/2, d4 u = -3/4 (mod 1).
  From the first, u = (-1/4 + m)/d2 ; substituting forces d3/d2 = 2 and d4/d2 = 3.
  direction        does the geodesic hit a centre EXACTLY?   min sup-dist to a centre
  (1, 2, 3)        YES   (aligned)                            0.00000
  (2, 4, 6)        YES   (aligned)                            0.00000
